From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: agrucza <a.grucza@gmx.net>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 09:10:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] platform: arm64: add the ASUS ProArt PZ13 embedded controller
 driver

The Snapdragon X Plus based ASUS ProArt PZ13 has an ASUS embedded
controller on I2C (0x5b) that drives the fan. The EC does not measure the
SoC; its fan curve runs on a temperature the OS writes through the EC's
command interface (RAM offset 0x83, plus a "temperature valid" flag), which
is what the ASUS platform software does on the original OS. Without it the
fan never starts: the SoC reached 72 degrees under load with the fan off.

Report the hottest of the thermal zones listed in the device tree to the EC
once a second, and provide the fan speed, the EC's two temperature sensors
and the reported temperature via hwmon. A floor temperature below the EC's
curve is reported on suspend so the fan does not run through it.

The EC's curve is tame: about 4100 rpm at a reported 84 degrees, 4600 at
90, while the fan does 9700 with the EC's full-speed bit (the "CPU fan
control" switch of the ASUS WMI interface), and the SoC's thermal zones
carry no passive trip. So set that bit once the reported temperature
reaches 85 degrees and clear it again below 75 (measured: 9626 rpm the
moment 85 was reported, back on the curve after the load), clear it for
suspend, and adopt its state at probe so that a driver reload does not
leave it set forever.

Signed-off-by: agrucza <a.grucza@gmx.net>
[birk: Kconfig and Makefile context for this kernel]
Signed-off-by: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
---
 .../asus,proart-pz13-ec.yaml                  |  64 +++
 drivers/platform/arm64/Kconfig                |  13 +
 drivers/platform/arm64/Makefile               |   1 +
 drivers/platform/arm64/asus-proart-pz13-ec.c  | 482 ++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 560 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/embedded-controller/asus,proart-pz13-ec.yaml
 create mode 100644 drivers/platform/arm64/asus-proart-pz13-ec.c

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/embedded-controller/asus,proart-pz13-ec.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/embedded-controller/asus,proart-pz13-ec.yaml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e12425e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/embedded-controller/asus,proart-pz13-ec.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,64 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0-only OR BSD-2-Clause)
+%YAML 1.2
+---
+$id: http://devicetree.org/schemas/embedded-controller/asus,proart-pz13-ec.yaml#
+$schema: http://devicetree.org/meta-schemas/core.yaml#
+
+title: ASUS ProArt PZ13 Embedded Controller
+
+maintainers:
+  - Alex Grucza <a.grucza@gmx.net>
+
+description:
+  The Qualcomm Snapdragon-based ASUS ProArt PZ13 tablet has an embedded
+  controller on I2C that drives the fan. The EC does not measure the SoC
+  itself; it runs its fan curve on a temperature the operating system writes
+  to it, the hottest of the SoC's thermal sensors. The EC also reports the
+  fan speed and two of its own temperature sensors.
+
+properties:
+  compatible:
+    const: asus,proart-pz13-ec
+
+  reg:
+    const: 0x5b
+
+  asus,thermal-zones:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle-array
+    items:
+      maxItems: 1
+    description:
+      Thermal zones whose hottest temperature is reported to the EC.
+
+required:
+  - compatible
+  - reg
+  - asus,thermal-zones
+
+additionalProperties: false
+
+examples:
+  - |
+    thermal-zones {
+        cpu_thermal: cpu-thermal {
+            thermal-sensors = <&tsens 1>;
+            trips { };
+        };
+
+        gpu_thermal: gpu-thermal {
+            thermal-sensors = <&tsens 2>;
+            trips { };
+        };
+    };
+
+    i2c {
+        #address-cells = <1>;
+        #size-cells = <0>;
+
+        embedded-controller@5b {
+            compatible = "asus,proart-pz13-ec";
+            reg = <0x5b>;
+            asus,thermal-zones = <&cpu_thermal>, <&gpu_thermal>;
+        };
+    };
+...
